WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:04.859
The last season of Game of Thrones was always
going to feature plenty of death, destruction,

00:00:04.859 --> 00:00:09.390
and chaos, and it certainly didn't disappoint
with its penultimate episode, "The Bells,"

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:13.390
which focuses almost entirely on the long-awaited
siege of King's Landing.

00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:17.460
With the end in sight, the series still has
plenty of plots left to conclude, and it moved

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:19.570
closer than ever to the endgame.

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:23.599
With the final episode just a week away, the
show is offing major characters left and right

00:00:23.599 --> 00:00:27.070
- let's dive into who didn't win the Game
of Thrones this time around.

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:29.800
Obviously gigantic spoilers ahead.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:33.640
Lord Varys has been one of the most mysterious
figures on Game of Thrones throughout its

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:34.660
run.

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:38.300
The best gossip in the Seven Kingdoms, Varys
quietly pulled the strings in the background

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:42.290
for much of the show's eight seasons, even
as many of the main characters surrounding

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:44.510
him thought they were calling the shots.

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:48.650
Until the very end, Varys was consistent and
pragmatic about who might be the best ruler

00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:49.990
of the Seven Kingdoms.

00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:53.900
And once he found out that Jon Snow had a
stronger claim to the Iron Throne than Daenerys

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:57.510
Targaryen, he went against the Dragon Queen,
knowing that doing so would immediately put

00:00:57.510 --> 00:00:58.810
himself at risk.

00:00:58.810 --> 00:01:02.830
In trying to do what was best for the Seven
Kingdoms, The Spider signs his own death warrant,

00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:05.080
and finds himself at the mercy of Daenerys.

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:10.010
Unfortunately for him, she has little to no
mercy left to spare, and Varys dies by flame,

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:11.560
the latest victim of the word:

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:13.040
"Dracarys."

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:25.430
Game of Thrones has been quietly laying tracks
for Daenerys to follow in her unstable father's

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:29.710
footsteps for quite some time, but the Dragon
Queen's pivot to Mad Queen still seems quite

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:33.080
abrupt, even for a woman who's made a habit
of burning her enemies.

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:37.790
By the beginning of the fifth episode, Daenerys
is utterly despondent, having lost two dragons

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:42.140
as well as two of her closest friends and
confidantes Jorah Mormont and Missandei.

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:46.070
She seems to have lost her compass, and she
spends some of the episode's earlier moments

00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:50.220
threatening her Queen's Hand, Tyrion Lannister,
as well as trying to rekindle the romance

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:53.830
she had with Jon Snow before they learned
his secret royal lineage makes him a more

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:57.600
compelling contender for the Throne - as well
as the fact that she's his aunt.

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:04.080
Jon, although visibly conflicted, rejects
her romantic advances - probably because,

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:08.140
well, she's his aunt - a rejection that steels
Daenerys for her vengeful path.

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:11.800
Even though the bells of King's Landing ring
soon after Daenerys' first assault to signal

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:15.870
a full surrender to their new queen, she shows
no mercy to the city.

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:20.390
She sets both soldiers and civilians ablaze
in an ugly, horrific move that exhibits the

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:22.840
worst of her family's infamous impulses.

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:27.200
Without her trusted advisors, Daenerys has
run amok, and just to make everything worse,

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:30.099
she's massacred thousands of innocents in
the process.

00:02:30.099 --> 00:02:34.130
With so many citizens of King's Landing dying
in her assault, Queen Daenerys may not have

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:38.500
many people to actually rule when she finally
takes whatever's left of the throne.

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:42.000
It seems that Varys was right to have backed
Jon Snow after all...

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:45.880
One of the show's most highly anticipated
moments finally arrives in "The Bells."

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:50.380
We're talking, of course, about the long-awaited
battle known as CleganeBowl, the final showdown

00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:55.170
between the righteous yet savage Sandor Clegane,
known as the Hound, and his enormous, zombified

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:57.650
older brother Gregor, known as the Mountain.

00:02:57.650 --> 00:03:01.739
The two finally meet in the Red Keep as Cersei
tries to mount her escape, but neither brother

00:03:01.739 --> 00:03:05.959
gives a second thought to the Lannister queen,
who casually sidles away as the two finally

00:03:05.959 --> 00:03:07.280
prepare to face off.

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:11.540
The Mountain tosses Cersei's Hand, Qyburn,
aside like a rag doll and kills him, and the

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:12.710
battle begins.

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:16.510
After a brutal fight, during which the Hound
realizes he can't simply kill this creature

00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:20.510
who was once his brother, he tackles him as
the building collapses, leading both brothers

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:24.730
to fall to their deaths and providing a poignant
ending to the Clegane conflict as well as

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:26.440
the Hound's character arc.

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:31.040
The three remaining Lannisters - Jaime, Tyrion,
and Cersei - have spent the show's eight seasons

00:03:31.069 --> 00:03:33.069
at odds with each other more often than not.

00:03:33.069 --> 00:03:37.220
But in this episode, members of the fraught
family come back together more than once,

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:39.940
helping each other get through the war as
best as they can.

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:44.650
Before the battle begins, Tyrion frees Jaime
from captivity in his own camp, asking Jaime

00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:48.280
to make sure the bells of surrender ring,
and convince Cersei to escape from King's

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:52.310
Landing in a dinghy Tyrion has arranged to
have waiting in a secret spot on the shore.

00:03:52.310 --> 00:03:56.640
The two also share a beautifully tender moment
when Tyrion tells Jaime that he would never

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:58.490
have survived his childhood without him:

00:03:58.490 --> 00:04:04.240
"You were the only one who didn't treat me
like a monster."

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:12.040
Jaime repays Tyrion for his help, and at his
brother's urging, tries to escape with Cersei

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:15.849
after he fights and murders Euron Greyjoy
so he can find his way back to her side.

00:04:15.849 --> 00:04:19.900
But they soon discover there's no way out
as the Red Keep collapses above them.

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:23.400
The two meet their deaths in each other's
arms as the world falls apart around them,

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:27.280
proving that no matter what, the Lannisters
not only pay their debts, but stick together

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:28.460
until the bitter end.

